{
  "children": [
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            46,
            72
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "What an expression may say"
        }
      ],
      "depth": 1,
      "position": [
        44,
        72
      ],
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            74,
            352
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "MDVX is deliberately small: one expression compiles once and is evaluated per\nrow, it reads fields by bare name, and the only functions it can call are the\nwhitelisted ones. Everything below is one row's worth of arithmetic, and none\nof it can reach outside the row it is given."
        }
      ],
      "position": [
        74,
        352
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            354,
            389
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Precedence is the ordinary one, so "
        },
        {
          "position": [
            389,
            411
          ],
          "type": "inlineCode",
          "value": "units * price - cost"
        },
        {
          "position": [
            411,
            437
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": " needs no parentheses\nand "
        },
        {
          "position": [
            437,
            458
          ],
          "type": "inlineCode",
          "value": "(units - 2) * price"
        },
        {
          "position": [
            458,
            483
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": " cannot do without them. "
        },
        {
          "position": [
            483,
            487
          ],
          "type": "inlineCode",
          "value": "in"
        },
        {
          "position": [
            487,
            492
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": " and "
        },
        {
          "position": [
            492,
            502
          ],
          "type": "inlineCode",
          "value": "contains"
        },
        {
          "position": [
            502,
            560
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": " are\nspelled as words but are comparisons like any other, "
        },
        {
          "position": [
            560,
            564
          ],
          "type": "inlineCode",
          "value": "&&"
        },
        {
          "position": [
            564,
            584
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": " binds tighter than\n"
        },
        {
          "position": [
            584,
            588
          ],
          "type": "inlineCode",
          "value": "||"
        },
        {
          "position": [
            588,
            594
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": ", and "
        },
        {
          "position": [
            594,
            598
          ],
          "type": "inlineCode",
          "value": "if"
        },
        {
          "position": [
            598,
            713
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": " is a function rather than a syntax — which is why it takes its\ntwo branches as arguments and evaluates to a value."
        }
      ],
      "position": [
        354,
        713
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
